          "type": "concept",
          "title": "Ulm, 14 March 1879",
          "content": "**Albert Einstein** was born at **11:30 a.m. on Friday, 14 March 1879**, at Bahnhofstrasse B 135 in **Ulm**, in the Kingdom of Württemberg, German Empire. The empire itself was only eight years old: Bismarck's unification of 1871 was a fresh political fact, and Württemberg retained its own king under the federal constitution.\n\nHis parents were **Hermann Einstein** (1847–1902), a feather-bed merchant who had recently pivoted to electrical engineering, and **Pauline Koch** (1858–1920), the cultured daughter of a wealthy grain dealer from Cannstatt. The family was **Jewish but resolutely secular** — what historians of Central European Jewry call *Bildungsbürgertum*: cultured bourgeoisie who prized Goethe and Schiller over the Torah, and who had embraced the assimilationist promise of post-emancipation Germany.\n\nAlbert was their first child. A sister, **Maria (\"Maja\")**, would follow in 1881 and remain his closest sibling and confidante for life.\n\n**Within a year of Albert's birth, in summer 1880, the family moved to Munich.** Hermann and his younger brother **Jakob Einstein** — a trained engineer — were setting up an electrotechnical firm in the Bavarian capital, where the new technologies of direct-current power, dynamos, and arc lamps promised great fortunes.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">ULM, 14 MARCH 1879</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">A Swabian birth in the new German Empire</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"170\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"220\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-size=\"26\" font-weight=\"bold\">Vital statistics</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"262\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Born 11:30 a.m., Friday 14 March 1879</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"295\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Bahnhofstrasse B 135, Ulm, Kingdom of Württemberg</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"328\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">German Empire, age 8 (founded 1871)</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"410\" width=\"450\" height=\"280\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"460\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-size=\"26\" font-weight=\"bold\">Hermann Einstein</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"502\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">1847–1902</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"540\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Feather-bed merchant turned</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"572\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">electrical entrepreneur</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"620\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Warm, dreamy, financially</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"648\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">unlucky — qualities Albert</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"676\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">inherited.</text><rect x=\"570\" y=\"410\" width=\"450\" height=\"280\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.12)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"610\" y=\"460\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-size=\"26\" font-weight=\"bold\">Pauline Koch</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"502\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">1858–1920</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"540\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Daughter of Cannstatt grain</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"572\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">wealth; trained pianist</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"620\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Practical, musical,</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"648\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">socially ambitious. Pushed</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"676\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Albert toward violin at 5.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"730\" width=\"940\" height=\"290\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"780\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"26\" font-weight=\"bold\">A secular Jewish Bildungsbürger family</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"822\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Religion observed only nominally; Goethe and Schiller</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"855\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">on the shelf; assimilation the cultural project.</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"910\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Within 12 months the family decamps to Munich,</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"940\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">where Hermann and brother Jakob will found an</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"970\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">electrotechnical firm — Einstein &amp; Cie.</text></svg>",
            "caption": "The Einstein family at the moment of Albert's birth — secular, bourgeois, technologically ambitious."
          }
