          "explanation": "From the **\"Autobiographical Notes\"** (1949): *\"Something deeply hidden had to be behind things.\"* The compass becomes Einstein's founding myth of his own scientific realism — the conviction that lawful regularity points to a reality not exhausted by sense data. Read it carefully: at 70 he is **constructing** an origin story, but the epistemic moral is the same one that animates his 1905 willingness to take Maxwell's equations at their word.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">QUIZ — THE COMPASS MEMORY</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Reading the 1949 Autobiographical Notes</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"940\" height=\"240\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"232\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-size=\"26\" font-weight=\"bold\">Method note</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"278\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">A late-life memoir is a literary act, not a transcript.</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"316\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Ask: what is the writer trying to make of his past?</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"368\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Einstein at 70 is composing the prehistory of his own</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"396\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">epistemology, not testifying under oath.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"460\" width=\"940\" height=\"280\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"512\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-size=\"26\" font-weight=\"bold\">The key sentence</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"560\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">&quot;Something deeply hidden had to be behind things.&quot;</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"612\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Reality &gt; appearance.</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"650\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Law &gt; sensation.</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"688\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Field &gt; touch.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"780\" width=\"940\" height=\"240\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"830\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"26\" font-weight=\"bold\">Why it matters for 1905</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"876\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">The same realist instinct lets the 26-year-old patent</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"910\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">clerk take Maxwell's equations seriously enough to</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"944\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">scrap absolute time rather than fudge the math.</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"996\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Lorentz and Poincaré would not.</text></svg>",
            "caption": "A close reading of the compass passage as the prehistory of scientific realism."
          }
